WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:06.111
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.194 --> 00:08.030
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:09.448 --> 00:11.116
[in Korean] I like you.

5
00:42.272 --> 00:45.025
EPISODE 5

6
01:04.669 --> 01:07.172
[in English] Oh, why are you so heavy?

7
01:10.133 --> 01:13.345
Why did you have to eat 20 pounds of food for dinner?

8
01:13.428 --> 01:14.763
I didn't eat that much food!

9
01:15.722 --> 01:18.934
-[chuckles] Oh, you're awake? -If I'm so heavy, then put me down.

10
01:19.017 --> 01:21.687
-[in Korean] Okay, okay. -[in English] Put me down. Let go of me.

11
01:21.770 --> 01:24.189
-Drop me. Hey. -[in Korean] Okay!

12
01:24.272 --> 01:25.524
-[giggles] -[chuckles]

13
01:26.358 --> 01:27.359
[in English] Are you okay?

14
01:27.442 --> 01:29.194
-[in Korean] You all right? -I'm not all right.

15
01:29.277 --> 01:31.196
Wow, your Korean's getting better.

16
01:32.823 --> 01:34.282
[chuckles] Mmm.

17
01:38.704 --> 01:40.163
-Star. -Star.

18
01:41.373 --> 01:42.833
-Moon. -Moon.

19
01:43.875 --> 01:45.961
-Sky. -Sky. [chuckles]

20
01:48.839 --> 01:50.549
-Love. -Love.

21
01:51.800 --> 01:53.927
-Yubin. [chuckles] -Yubin.

22
01:56.221 --> 01:58.432
You know really beautiful words.

23
01:59.141 --> 02:00.892
Your turn. I'll test you.

24
02:00.976 --> 02:02.018
-Test me? -Mm-hmm.

25
02:02.561 --> 02:03.645
Uh…

26
02:04.604 --> 02:06.231
-Strawberry. -Wow.

27
02:06.940 --> 02:08.525
-Robber. -Hmm? [chuckles]

28
02:09.025 --> 02:10.861
-Airhead. -Airhead?

29
02:10.944 --> 02:11.945
Dummy.

30
02:12.028 --> 02:14.698
-[chuckling] What the heck? -[laughing]

31
02:16.074 --> 02:18.034
-Star. -Mm-hmm.

32
02:18.577 --> 02:20.162
-Moon. -Mm-hmm.

33
02:21.288 --> 02:22.873
-Sky. -Mm-hmm.

34
02:24.082 --> 02:25.083
Love.

35
02:27.085 --> 02:28.253
Karin.

36
02:50.525 --> 02:56.490
DEAR KARIN

37
03:35.654 --> 03:39.074
Why does Kunam always have to take things so seriously?

38
03:40.951 --> 03:43.453
-Your pronunciation's on point. -[chuckling]

39
03:43.537 --> 03:46.581
One for you. Here you are. Thanks for visiting us.

40
03:55.924 --> 03:59.261
Hey there, you here all by yourself? Wanna drink with the two of us?

41
03:59.344 --> 04:02.055
-No, thanks. I'm here with someone. -[scoffs] Doubt that.

42
04:02.556 --> 04:04.057
You've been here a whole hour

43
04:04.140 --> 04:06.142
-drinking by yourself. -I told you guys I'm not here alone.

44
04:06.226 --> 04:08.728
-Yeah, whatever. Sounds good. -Chill out and drink with us.

45
04:09.479 --> 04:10.730
A toast to us.

46
04:10.814 --> 04:12.524
-Cheers. [chuckles] -Cheers.

47
04:15.944 --> 04:18.989
You're in my seat. And you're talking to my girlfriend.

48
04:20.156 --> 04:23.243
-Really, dude? -Ah, man, I guess she's got a boyfriend.

49
04:23.326 --> 04:25.036
-Our bad. Yeah, sorry. -Hey. Sorry about that.

50
04:31.042 --> 04:33.628
Since when have you started calling me your girlfriend?

51
04:33.712 --> 04:35.547
Okay. Is calling you my boyfriend better?

52
04:39.009 --> 04:40.635
How did you know that I was here?

53
04:42.846 --> 04:47.058
By manner of deduction. I checked all the food stalls, one by one.

54
04:47.142 --> 04:49.311
#LONELY NIGHT - #FUKUOKA #FOOD STAND

55
04:55.400 --> 04:57.027
I can't believe you.

56
05:02.616 --> 05:03.783
Mari, are you…

57
05:04.659 --> 05:08.830
interested in me even a little?

58
05:13.335 --> 05:16.004
When I confessed my feelings, I…

59
05:17.964 --> 05:19.841
I wasn't joking around or anything.

60
05:25.055 --> 05:26.765
I meant what I said before.

61
05:29.643 --> 05:31.269
I've always been serious about you.

62
05:35.190 --> 05:38.151
Why do you always have to be so heavy about this?

63
05:39.110 --> 05:40.612
Like I said before,

64
05:40.695 --> 05:42.948
I just want to play and have fun.

65
05:44.115 --> 05:46.284
I don't mind, Mari, you can have fun.

66
05:47.202 --> 05:48.411
Let me be…

67
05:49.537 --> 05:50.538
the serious one.

68
05:52.791 --> 05:54.167
Do you think you can…

69
05:55.210 --> 05:56.753
give us a chance?

70
05:59.005 --> 06:02.008
Mari, you're here.

71
06:02.092 --> 06:05.303
A winning prize for Charo will make you happy, Mari.

72
06:05.387 --> 06:10.141
I really… Mari, I really like you a lot.

73
06:29.411 --> 06:33.540
When we're done with these drinks, that's when our relationship will begin.

74
06:46.678 --> 06:48.888
-[sighs, chuckles] -[chuckles]

75
06:59.441 --> 07:01.818
Mari, wait. Is… is this real?

76
07:22.172 --> 07:24.257
It hurts all over.

77
07:25.175 --> 07:27.051
I overdid it last night.

78
07:27.135 --> 07:29.929
You shocked me with how much strength you have, you know that?

79
07:31.097 --> 07:34.142
Well, I guess I'm more vigorous than I thought.

80
07:37.854 --> 07:40.648
You're the reason everything hurts so much!

81
07:46.863 --> 07:48.448
Hey, Mari, listen…

82
07:49.324 --> 07:50.909
Tonight I'm gonna…

83
07:52.035 --> 07:53.912
I'm gonna protect you.

84
07:57.707 --> 08:01.044
Whatever. What are you protecting me from?

85
08:02.504 --> 08:04.088
It's the other way around.

86
08:05.924 --> 08:07.550
-[grunting] -[groaning]

87
08:08.343 --> 08:09.886
Mari.

88
08:11.763 --> 08:16.309
[in English] I… I have no idea what you're saying. [exclaims]

89
08:18.269 --> 08:20.063
I'm sorry if I was annoying.

90
08:20.146 --> 08:21.481
I'm kind of a lightweight with alcohol.

91
08:21.564 --> 08:22.565
Mm-hmm.

92
08:23.650 --> 08:26.903
Hey, by the way, what does "Nan neo-bak-ae-oep-seo" mean?

93
08:28.071 --> 08:29.656
It means, "You're my one and only."

94
08:31.366 --> 08:33.701
All right. Keep massaging with vigor.

95
08:33.785 --> 08:34.953
Aye-aye.

96
08:35.036 --> 08:36.329
-Right here? -Mm-hmm.

97
08:44.212 --> 08:46.339
-[door opens] -[footsteps approaching]

98
08:52.053 --> 08:54.389
-[knocks] -Oh. [chuckles]

99
08:54.472 --> 08:56.015
What are you doing over there?

100
08:56.099 --> 08:57.100
Ah.

101
08:58.226 --> 08:59.561
-Coffee. -Ah.

102
09:14.242 --> 09:15.243
DEAR KARIN

103
09:28.923 --> 09:31.718
What kind of relationship do we have?

104
09:38.892 --> 09:44.230
Korea… Dating… Start dating…

105
09:45.231 --> 09:46.357
What to know.

106
09:51.654 --> 09:52.655
Huh?

107
09:52.739 --> 09:54.866
THE REAL KOREAN DATING CULTURE DISPLAYING AFFECTION

108
09:54.949 --> 09:57.744
"In Korea, there are steps before becoming official." What's that mean?

109
09:57.827 --> 10:01.706
DATING STARTS WITH AN AMBIGUOUS RELATIONSHIP

110
10:01.789 --> 10:05.960
"The In-between phase is called… Sseom?"

111
10:09.172 --> 10:13.551
"Don't be overly affectionate. Make sure to keep the right amount of space."

112
10:19.098 --> 10:20.558
How? We live together.

113
10:26.981 --> 10:29.234
WHAT MAKES KOREAN MEN ATTRACTIVE &amp; THE PROS OF DATING ONE

114
10:29.317 --> 10:31.319
"Only be physical after you're official."

115
10:31.402 --> 10:32.779
[gasps] Wait a minute.

116
10:38.117 --> 10:39.369
Then are we…

117
10:39.911 --> 10:41.371
-[chief] Karin. -Who's there?

118
10:41.454 --> 10:42.789
[exclaims] Oh, Chief.

119
10:42.872 --> 10:44.666
I'm sorry. Did I scare you?

120
10:44.749 --> 10:46.292
It's all right. [grunts]

121
10:46.376 --> 10:48.127
Can I help you with something?

122
10:48.211 --> 10:50.338
Actually, I came to ask a favor.

123
10:52.465 --> 10:54.217
[in Korean] All right, this one…

124
10:55.426 --> 10:56.803
And for dinner…

125
10:59.097 --> 11:01.266
What should I make… Oh.

126
11:01.349 --> 11:02.892
Karin! Karin. Karin.

127
11:03.601 --> 11:05.019
-[in English] Huh? -Want to take a break?

128
11:05.103 --> 11:06.187
Hmm? What?

129
11:06.271 --> 11:07.772
[in Korean] Hold on a sec.

130
11:07.855 --> 11:09.732
[in English] Oh, where-where are you going?

131
11:09.816 --> 11:12.235
-Out. The, uh… The Chief said that… -Huh?

132
11:12.318 --> 11:14.404
-a… a visitor has just arrived… -Yeah, yeah, yeah. Yes?

133
11:14.487 --> 11:17.115
…and he wants me to give them a tour of the village.

134
11:17.198 --> 11:19.701
Oh. You want me to come with you?

135
11:21.703 --> 11:25.081
THE RIGHT AMOUNT OF SPACE

136
11:26.541 --> 11:28.459
No, no, no. Yubin, I need you here.

137
11:28.543 --> 11:30.503
-We have so much work to do here, right? -Ah.

138
11:30.586 --> 11:32.505
-Um, the bugs in the field… -Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

139
11:32.588 --> 11:34.924
-Oh, the bugs. -Please pick them with your hands. Okay?

140
11:35.008 --> 11:36.342
-With my hands. -Mm-hmm.

141
11:37.635 --> 11:39.470
Ah. Oh, Karin!

142
11:40.263 --> 11:42.682
You and I can have our dinner together?

143
11:44.350 --> 11:46.811
Mm-hmm, sounds good. See you later then!

144
11:51.983 --> 11:55.111
I pick the bugs with my hands. Pick the bugs every day, pick the bugs.

145
11:55.194 --> 11:56.904
[in Korean] Well, then…

146
12:05.038 --> 12:06.539
It's worn out.

147
12:07.832 --> 12:10.418
How many times did someone bump into this

148
12:11.210 --> 12:13.046
for it to look like this?

149
12:15.006 --> 12:16.215
Wait a minute…

150
12:23.431 --> 12:26.017
CHARO VILLAGE OFFICE

151
12:31.773 --> 12:34.233
-Thank you for the ride. I appreciate it! -[chief] Of course.

152
12:38.988 --> 12:42.241
She mentioned that she was here for some kinda resort planning business.

153
12:43.159 --> 12:45.244
-A resort business? -Mm-hmm.

154
12:45.328 --> 12:48.122
She came all this way and said she wanted to take a tour.

155
12:48.206 --> 12:49.540
Ooh.

156
12:49.624 --> 12:52.377
So thanks for showing her around.

157
12:52.460 --> 12:54.837
-Of course. -I can't do it because of this.

158
12:55.588 --> 12:57.090
Seems to scare a lot of people off.

159
12:58.716 --> 13:01.094
-Ah, I see. [chuckles] -[chuckles]

160
13:01.177 --> 13:02.428
Happy to help.

161
13:02.512 --> 13:04.222
Where should our first stop be?

162
13:04.305 --> 13:05.807
Ah! We're over here!

163
13:22.407 --> 13:23.991
-Hello there. -Hi.

164
13:24.075 --> 13:25.410
Hello there.

165
13:25.493 --> 13:27.203
Are you my tour guide around the island?

166
13:27.286 --> 13:30.248
Uh, yes. Shirahama Karin. It's a pleasure.

167
13:30.873 --> 13:32.500
I'm Han Sia.

168
13:33.000 --> 13:34.210
I flew here from Korea.

169
13:35.878 --> 13:38.756
Ah. You can speak comfortably, I'll understand you.

170
13:41.467 --> 13:44.512
[in Korean] I can… speak… a little bit.

171
13:46.139 --> 13:50.017
[in English] Wow. Well then, where do you suggest we begin my tour today?

172
13:50.101 --> 13:53.437
Don't worry. You can leave everything to me. [chuckles]

173
13:53.980 --> 13:55.606
We'll be on our way then.

174
14:03.406 --> 14:05.449
[in Korean] What should I make?

175
14:15.501 --> 14:16.961
There it is!

176
14:17.044 --> 14:20.089
-[in English] Oh. Excuse me, ma'am. -[chuckles] It's all right.

177
14:20.173 --> 14:22.758
-It's all yours. You can have it. -[chuckles] Oh, the meat is mine?

178
14:22.842 --> 14:24.677
-Oh, thank you very much. -Yeah.

179
14:24.760 --> 14:26.470
This one? Or this one?

180
14:26.554 --> 14:28.723
The slices are much thicker on that one.

181
14:29.223 --> 14:30.641
-Oh. -Mmm, go with that one.

182
14:30.725 --> 14:32.268
-Oh? -I'd say it really takes the cake.

183
14:32.351 --> 14:34.562
-You like this? This one "takes the cake"? -Mmm. It'll be the best.

184
14:36.063 --> 14:39.442
I took this little alleyway every morning to school and back

185
14:39.525 --> 14:40.735
when I was a young student.

186
14:40.818 --> 14:44.697
-Oh, Mr. Sato. Hi. [chuckles] -Hey, Karin. [chuckles] Hi.

187
14:44.780 --> 14:47.825
-I'm giving her a tour. [chuckles] -[Mr. Sato] Mmm.

188
14:49.744 --> 14:52.496
As you can see, the people of this island are incredibly kind

189
14:52.580 --> 14:55.041
-and supportive of each other. -[shutter clicks]

190
14:57.585 --> 14:59.837
This area is known for its beautiful scenery.

191
14:59.921 --> 15:02.089
In the summer, people come to this popular spot

192
15:02.173 --> 15:04.634
to enjoy the vibrant blue hue of the water against the sky.

193
15:05.259 --> 15:07.803
Our communities come together to help and support each other

194
15:07.887 --> 15:09.180
as we grow various crops.

195
15:09.889 --> 15:10.890
What else?

196
15:11.807 --> 15:13.184
Let's go to the next stop.

197
15:17.521 --> 15:20.358
I can't tell if she's interested in our island or not.

198
15:39.335 --> 15:40.711
[in Korean] Mix it up real good.

199
15:43.881 --> 15:45.091
That's done.

200
15:48.761 --> 15:52.598
It's kind of bland… Let's see. Where's the salt? I'll add a dash of salt.

201
15:59.021 --> 16:01.607
What's that building over there?

202
16:03.317 --> 16:05.069
Oh, that's the community center.

203
16:06.237 --> 16:07.571
That's nice and central.

204
16:09.156 --> 16:11.659
It'll make a great food court or a café.

205
16:13.703 --> 16:15.955
It's central to all who live here.

206
16:16.747 --> 16:18.833
That's why it's our community center.

207
16:18.916 --> 16:19.917
That's cool.

208
16:21.752 --> 16:23.879
[in Korean] Just a bunch of old people…

209
16:29.051 --> 16:32.388
So, why live in the middle of nowhere?

210
16:32.471 --> 16:34.015
Isn't it suffocating to you?

211
16:34.765 --> 16:36.225
No, not at all.

212
16:36.934 --> 16:39.729
Quite the opposite actually. Living here clears my mind.

213
16:41.564 --> 16:44.525
Aren't you lonely living here when you're so young?

214
16:44.608 --> 16:46.986
There's nobody to hang out with and no clubs to go to.

215
16:50.573 --> 16:54.452
Believe it or not, there's a lot more here than you think.

216
16:56.120 --> 16:59.165
It's only something you learn the longer you spend time here.

217
16:59.248 --> 17:02.585
Hmm… I'll just have to take your word for it.

218
17:04.879 --> 17:08.132
There is actually one last place that I'd like to check out.

219
17:09.300 --> 17:10.426
Sure. Where's that?

220
17:11.052 --> 17:13.596
According to this, it should be right next to us.

221
17:14.221 --> 17:15.890
Oh. It's right over there.

222
17:26.609 --> 17:27.610
[in Korean] All right.

223
17:33.449 --> 17:34.992
Whew, all done.

224
17:37.161 --> 17:38.329
Ah.

225
17:43.459 --> 17:44.460
Now it's ready.

226
17:49.757 --> 17:50.758
[in English] Um, so…

227
17:51.592 --> 17:53.219
This place is…

228
17:53.302 --> 17:56.555
That's my house over there and my farm is right here.

229
17:58.099 --> 18:00.267
[in Korean] No wonder Lee Yubin's got his eye on this place.

230
18:04.814 --> 18:05.898
[in English] Welcome back!

231
18:06.691 --> 18:07.858
Hi.

232
18:08.526 --> 18:10.152
[in Korean] Is that you, Yubin?

233
18:12.446 --> 18:15.991
What are you doing here?

234
18:21.706 --> 18:22.707
Oh. [sighs]

235
18:30.923 --> 18:32.383
So he's living here?

236
18:40.641 --> 18:42.810
He's still designing stuff.

237
18:55.114 --> 18:57.074
Something's changed.

238
19:03.706 --> 19:08.169
FIVE YEARS AGO

239
19:13.758 --> 19:17.303
How many nights have you spent staying up?

240
19:17.386 --> 19:19.889
How can I get any work done at home?

241
19:20.473 --> 19:21.474
Fair point.

242
19:24.685 --> 19:25.936
[Yubin] Go home before me.

243
19:28.564 --> 19:31.567
Your designs are right up my alley.

244
19:31.650 --> 19:33.736
Get out of here already.

245
19:33.819 --> 19:36.864
Still not interested in joining our company?

246
19:36.947 --> 19:38.365
I'm not interested.

247
19:38.449 --> 19:42.203
We can meet pretty much all your terms.

248
19:42.286 --> 19:46.624
I want to design freely without any meddling in my way.

249
19:47.625 --> 19:49.460
Ugh. You're such a handful.

250
19:52.379 --> 19:53.380
And I love that.

251
19:56.091 --> 19:59.470
You're not making any sense.

252
19:59.553 --> 20:01.430
Compared to before…

253
20:02.765 --> 20:04.308
his designs have become warmer.

254
20:30.626 --> 20:32.545
I heard you were negotiating.

255
20:33.712 --> 20:36.048
But I had no idea you were boarding here.

256
20:37.466 --> 20:41.220
I mean… It's not exactly boarding.

257
20:41.720 --> 20:44.598
It just… worked out that way.

258
20:45.641 --> 20:48.060
What are you doing here?

259
20:48.143 --> 20:49.854
I came here to help you out.

260
20:50.938 --> 20:52.273
I'll buy that land off you.

261
20:52.356 --> 20:54.191
My land?

262
20:55.943 --> 20:57.361
That's…

263
21:01.115 --> 21:03.576
You said that you made us dinner?

264
21:12.543 --> 21:14.837
Are you sure it doesn't bother you that I'm staying for dinner?

265
21:15.588 --> 21:16.672
Of course it doesn't.

266
21:17.381 --> 21:19.967
Yubin, Sia's an acquaintance of yours, right?

267
21:20.843 --> 21:23.095
-[chuckles] You two are friends? -[Yubin] Huh?

268
21:23.721 --> 21:25.639
Uh, um, the two of us are not.

269
21:25.723 --> 21:27.641
-She's my work-- -I had a crush on him.

270
21:28.392 --> 21:32.062
I used to be madly in love with Yubin, but it was one-sided.

271
21:32.146 --> 21:36.358
You see, I'm the girl who has always gotten whatever it is that I wanted.

272
21:36.442 --> 21:40.029
Unfortunately for me, Yubin's the only exception to that.

273
21:41.822 --> 21:45.200
[in Korean] Did you say something weird?

274
21:45.284 --> 21:47.119
I was just telling the truth.

275
21:53.709 --> 21:57.004
How long do you plan on staying here?

276
21:57.087 --> 21:58.964
I've got it handled. Just eat your food and go.

277
22:05.179 --> 22:08.098
[in English] Listen, Karin, this might be beyond your comprehension.

278
22:09.099 --> 22:13.479
Yubin isn't the type of person who belongs somewhere like this.

279
22:14.730 --> 22:16.190
What do you…

280
22:17.024 --> 22:18.651
Wait, uh, ho-ho-hold on.

281
22:19.944 --> 22:23.656
Karin, I'll… help her leave. Mmm.

282
22:23.739 --> 22:25.824
What? You mean now?

283
22:25.908 --> 22:27.451
Yes, I mean now.

284
22:27.534 --> 22:29.578
-[in Korean] Come on. Stand up. -[Sia] Ugh, why?

285
22:29.662 --> 22:31.789
[in English] Thanks for the tour today. It's been fun.

286
22:31.872 --> 22:32.957
[in Korean] Out you go.

287
22:33.040 --> 22:35.292
[in English] Oh, uh. Back in a second.

288
22:44.843 --> 22:46.470
[Mari] Hello. Welcome.

289
22:48.514 --> 22:49.932
[in Korean] What a gaudy shop.

290
22:53.102 --> 22:54.812
We'll have two draft beers, please.

291
22:54.895 --> 22:55.896
[Mari] Sure.

292
23:01.568 --> 23:03.696
I'll cut right to the chase.

293
23:04.655 --> 23:07.366
I'm not selling that property.

294
23:07.449 --> 23:10.494
Then what's your plan?

295
23:14.081 --> 23:16.083
Are you willing to give up your career?

296
23:17.876 --> 23:19.795
[in English] Please enjoy your drinks.

297
23:27.761 --> 23:30.264
[in Korean] Just sell it off to me.

298
23:30.973 --> 23:32.558
I'll buy it from you.

299
23:33.058 --> 23:35.310
Just sell it off

300
23:36.145 --> 23:38.147
and come back to Korea with me.

301
23:38.230 --> 23:41.608
You need the money to get back on your own feet.

302
23:41.692 --> 23:43.027
That's none of your business.

303
23:43.110 --> 23:47.072
I can't let my senior's talent go to waste in a place like this.

304
23:47.781 --> 23:49.116
I'd hate to see that.

305
24:02.212 --> 24:04.089
Mari, hi. Done with work already?

306
24:04.173 --> 24:06.091
I couldn't breathe in there. I had to leave.

307
24:06.175 --> 24:08.719
I seriously thought I was going to pass out or something.

308
24:08.802 --> 24:10.596
-Did something happen? -Yeah. Yubin.

309
24:10.679 --> 24:13.265
-He suddenly showed up with a weird woman. -A weird woman?

310
24:13.348 --> 24:15.434
And their intense vibe was something else!

311
24:15.517 --> 24:17.227
-Like our vibe is? -How can you joke around

312
24:17.311 --> 24:18.645
at a time like this?

313
24:18.729 --> 24:20.439
There's definitely something wrong.

314
24:20.522 --> 24:22.399
The energy felt so off and dark.

315
24:22.983 --> 24:24.860
Almost as if she's his…

316
24:25.819 --> 24:27.821
-[gasps] …his ex-girlfriend! -His loan shark!

317
24:27.905 --> 24:28.989
-What? -Huh?

318
24:31.033 --> 24:33.327
When he got here, Yubin said he lost all his money.

319
24:33.410 --> 24:34.953
That's gotta be why she's here.

320
24:35.037 --> 24:36.413
She's collecting her cash.

321
24:36.497 --> 24:39.083
You didn't see them. That definitely can't be it.

322
24:40.125 --> 24:41.960
[groans] What should I do?

323
24:43.253 --> 24:45.798
I got it! Kunam, keep an eye on them, okay?

324
24:45.881 --> 24:47.257
Oh, wait!

325
24:47.341 --> 24:50.385
If she tries to leave or anything, run over there and make sure she pays.

326
24:50.469 --> 24:51.678
You got it.

327
25:00.479 --> 25:03.065
Wasn't he helping her leave? Where the heck did he go?

328
25:03.816 --> 25:05.192
The ferry terminal?

329
25:05.275 --> 25:06.860
[scoffs] Or the airport?

330
25:07.528 --> 25:09.738
Wait a minute, he couldn't have gone to Korea…

331
25:12.032 --> 25:13.242
What's Yubin doing?

332
25:13.325 --> 25:16.161
He said he'd be back in a second. It's been longer than that.

333
25:16.745 --> 25:18.997
Karin. Karin? Karin!

334
25:19.081 --> 25:21.166
-Karin, Karin, hey… Karin. -Oh, Mari…

335
25:21.250 --> 25:22.793
-There's something I have to share. -Huh?

336
25:22.876 --> 25:24.002
Hurry. [stuttering]

337
25:24.086 --> 25:25.921
-Hurry and finish washing so we can talk. -What?

338
25:27.047 --> 25:28.715
A crush on Yubin?

339
25:28.799 --> 25:30.259
She said that to your face?

340
25:30.342 --> 25:31.343
[Karin] Mmm.

341
25:31.885 --> 25:34.555
She said it out of nowhere while we were eating.

342
25:35.305 --> 25:38.600
And then she started speaking to him in Korean, so I don't know what else…

343
25:38.684 --> 25:40.394
That was so rude of her.

344
25:40.477 --> 25:42.938
I bet she brought that up on purpose to bother you.

345
25:43.021 --> 25:45.941
"We have a special connection, and there's nothing you can do about it."

346
25:47.901 --> 25:50.571
-You think so? -Why else would she bring that up to you?

347
25:53.240 --> 25:54.324
Yeah, but…

348
25:55.159 --> 25:57.911
they looked like they've known each other forever, and…

349
25:58.829 --> 25:59.830
It felt as if…

350
26:00.664 --> 26:02.583
I was intruding on their conversation.

351
26:02.666 --> 26:05.878
What? Karin, what are you saying?

352
26:05.961 --> 26:09.590
She's the one trying to come in between you and Yubin. You know that.

353
26:10.340 --> 26:11.633
Come between…

354
26:15.888 --> 26:17.556
You thought I couldn't tell?

355
26:18.348 --> 26:19.850
Anybody with eyes can see it.

356
26:23.770 --> 26:26.857
You and Yubin have something special going on.

357
26:29.985 --> 26:33.447
Karin, I noticed the warm way Yubin looks and acts towards you.

358
26:33.530 --> 26:36.033
He gets all awkward and kind of sweet.

359
26:37.117 --> 26:40.204
But when he's around her, he becomes someone else.

360
26:40.287 --> 26:42.122
Someone stern and cold.

361
26:42.206 --> 26:43.790
I mean, it was weird.

362
26:43.874 --> 26:47.127
The energy was so awkward and tense that I had to leave.

363
26:48.670 --> 26:50.881
Okay? Don't let her get to you.

364
27:01.934 --> 27:03.769
Do you wanna know something fun?

365
27:04.353 --> 27:06.855
I'm gonna tell you what scares her type the most.

366
27:07.773 --> 27:08.774
What is it?

367
27:10.400 --> 27:12.444
Open up to her about how you feel.

368
27:13.362 --> 27:15.822
Face her directly and openly.

369
27:23.455 --> 27:24.998
I don't really get it.

370
27:25.958 --> 27:27.042
Get what?

371
27:31.463 --> 27:32.923
What if we…

372
27:35.550 --> 27:38.845
Maybe Yubin and I were incompatible from the very start.

373
27:40.347 --> 27:41.598
From the very start?

374
27:41.682 --> 27:43.850
Do you even know when that was, exactly?

375
27:44.601 --> 27:46.395
Obstacles like nationality, age, etcetera,

376
27:46.478 --> 27:48.814
can all be overcome by honest love, right?

377
27:49.523 --> 27:54.486
What I'm not sure of is whether or not Yubin is serious about a relationship.

378
27:55.153 --> 27:58.949
[sighs] And Sia is a lot more impressive than me in every way.

379
28:02.953 --> 28:04.121
Remember the card I pulled?

380
28:05.956 --> 28:08.333
At the bus terminal where you and Yubin met?

381
28:08.417 --> 28:10.585
Because I think it's about time you pay attention to it.

382
28:11.837 --> 28:14.965
It's the Wheel of Fortune.

383
28:15.465 --> 28:17.551
It means you're bound to have a fated encounter

384
28:17.634 --> 28:20.178
camouflaged as a coincidence in the near future.

385
28:23.932 --> 28:26.101
Mmm. I remember it.

386
28:26.184 --> 28:28.353
If he appears before you as if it were meant to be,

387
28:28.437 --> 28:29.813
maybe it's not a coincidence.

388
28:30.397 --> 28:33.483
But it's up to you to decide whether he's the one for you or not.

389
28:34.443 --> 28:35.777
Is that a bad thing?

390
28:36.695 --> 28:37.988
The outcome would be up to you.

391
28:38.739 --> 28:40.365
It's your choice.

392
28:41.992 --> 28:43.285
Okay?

393
28:45.704 --> 28:47.372
Strawberries and romance.

394
28:47.873 --> 28:49.833
They're a lot more alike than you think.

395
28:50.333 --> 28:53.879
The more love and care that you pour in, the sweeter they get, right?

396
28:53.962 --> 28:55.547
So don't be afraid of it.

397
29:17.694 --> 29:19.863
[in Korean] I'll think it over.

398
29:21.907 --> 29:22.949
Get home safe.

399
29:23.909 --> 29:24.910
I already missed my ferry.

400
29:26.244 --> 29:27.412
What should I do?

401
29:28.288 --> 29:29.372
How should I know?

402
29:29.456 --> 29:32.250
Let me stay with you. I don't mind if we share a room.

403
29:32.334 --> 29:34.586
-Wait… -[Mari] I have a place you can stay.

404
29:39.716 --> 29:41.384
-[Sia, in English] Oh, wait, wait… -Bye!

405
29:42.928 --> 29:45.680
-[in Korean] Hey! -[in English] Stop yappin' so much!

406
29:45.764 --> 29:48.391
Hey, young lady. You're way too loud.

407
29:54.564 --> 29:56.775
Lay down and relax, dear.

408
29:57.317 --> 30:00.237
Don't pay us elder ladies any mind, all right?

409
30:01.071 --> 30:02.823
Have you eaten dinner yet?

410
30:03.615 --> 30:05.450
Would you like me to make some soba?

411
30:17.963 --> 30:19.297
[Sia, in Korean] It's all about timing.

412
30:19.381 --> 30:20.799
Even as we speak,

413
30:20.882 --> 30:26.054
new competition is constantly emerging to take your place, Lee Yubin.

414
30:27.222 --> 30:28.765
But you know that better than I do.

415
30:30.016 --> 30:33.145
I could get you on a new project through some investors I know.

416
30:33.228 --> 30:36.773
Getting your name out there again? It really isn't that hard, you know.

417
30:36.857 --> 30:39.317
Don't make it sound easy.

418
30:39.401 --> 30:40.610
But it is easy.

419
30:41.236 --> 30:44.865
You've got the talent, and I've got the money.

420
30:46.658 --> 30:47.826
As an entrepreneur,

421
30:47.909 --> 30:50.328
I am here to make an offer

422
30:50.412 --> 30:52.998
to Lee Yubin, the spatial designer.

423
30:55.000 --> 30:58.295
I'm busy too. I won't wait around.

424
31:13.894 --> 31:15.270
[in English] Hey, Yubin. Come here.

425
31:15.353 --> 31:17.397
The sugar levels have finally risen.

426
31:17.480 --> 31:18.815
-Look at that. -[in Korean] Let's see.

427
31:19.357 --> 31:20.942
-[chuckles] -Are you that happy?

428
31:21.026 --> 31:23.403
-So very happy! [chuckles] -[chuckling]

429
31:28.825 --> 31:30.493
[in English] Just trust me.

430
31:31.119 --> 31:33.872
-[chuckles] -[cheers, laughs]

431
33:20.145 --> 33:21.646
[in Korean] Did you see the photos?

432
33:22.647 --> 33:26.318
The view and the space aren't bad, are they?

433
33:26.401 --> 33:30.196
We could just bulldoze over everything.

434
33:33.450 --> 33:34.701
Well, I'll see you in Korea.

435
33:45.795 --> 33:47.547
-Karin, wait a second. -Hmm?

436
33:48.298 --> 33:50.133
-Wear this. -[in English] Uh…

437
33:50.216 --> 33:51.426
You keep it, Yubin.

438
33:51.509 --> 33:53.178
No, you need to wear it.

439
33:53.678 --> 33:55.013
-It's chilly. -Mmm.

440
33:55.096 --> 33:57.307
It's breezy. The wind is cold.

441
33:59.517 --> 34:00.769
-[in Korean] There. -[Karin] Thank you.

442
34:01.478 --> 34:02.771
What's with that smile?

443
34:08.151 --> 34:09.778
[in English] Good morning, everybody.

444
34:11.905 --> 34:12.906
Uh…

445
34:16.368 --> 34:17.744
Good morning.

446
34:18.828 --> 34:21.956
How long are you planning on staying with us, Sia?

447
34:23.208 --> 34:24.292
I'm on my way out.

448
34:25.168 --> 34:26.378
But I figured…

449
34:27.712 --> 34:29.130
while I'm here…

450
34:31.299 --> 34:33.968
Yubin and I could grab a coffee before my ferry leaves.

451
34:34.052 --> 34:37.180
[in Korean] Hey, what are you doing?

452
34:43.770 --> 34:44.896
HYEJIN

453
34:51.403 --> 34:53.279
[Hyejin] It's urgent. Pick up your phone.

454
35:02.497 --> 35:05.959
[in English] Why don't we all just grab a coffee together at Serendipity?

455
35:06.042 --> 35:07.460
I'd love to treat you both.

456
35:07.961 --> 35:09.629
-[chuckles] -[scoffs]

457
35:11.589 --> 35:12.716
Sure, why not?

458
35:13.633 --> 35:16.386
There is actually something I wanted to tell you anyway.

459
35:17.470 --> 35:19.597
-[Yubin] Uh, Karin… -Hmm?

460
35:19.681 --> 35:22.517
Um, why don't you two go on ahead?

461
35:23.893 --> 35:25.729
I'll head over after my call.

462
35:26.604 --> 35:28.773
-Mmm. Don't take too long. -[Yubin] Okay.

463
35:31.401 --> 35:35.363
[in Korean] You better leave after you drink your coffee, okay?

464
35:35.447 --> 35:37.323
[in English] Mmm. Don't take too long.

465
35:52.881 --> 35:54.758
I set an alarm for when you need to leave.

466
35:54.841 --> 35:57.218
We wouldn't want you to miss your ferry a second time, would we?

467
36:12.901 --> 36:13.902
All right, Sia.

468
36:15.904 --> 36:20.074
Tell me the real reason that you came to Charo Island.

469
36:22.786 --> 36:27.791
I will. But first, I want you to tell me how close you and Yubin really are.

470
36:27.874 --> 36:28.917
Sorry?

471
36:29.626 --> 36:31.211
How long have you known him?

472
36:33.046 --> 36:36.424
I've known Yubin for almost an entire decade now.

473
36:39.636 --> 36:43.348
Are you even aware of the career Yubin had? How big he was?

474
36:47.477 --> 36:48.603
That's…

475
36:52.273 --> 36:57.153
Karin, don't tell me that you don't actually know why it is that he's here.

476
36:59.155 --> 37:00.156
He told me…

477
37:01.199 --> 37:03.284
He ran into a bit of trouble in Korea

478
37:03.368 --> 37:05.203
-so he needed to step away-- -He came to Charo Island

479
37:05.286 --> 37:06.871
because he wants to buy your land.

480
37:09.999 --> 37:11.000
What?

481
37:11.501 --> 37:12.836
[in Korean] What are you talking about?

482
37:13.628 --> 37:15.630
[Hyejin] Did you not know about this?

483
37:15.713 --> 37:21.678
I hear Sia is already negotiating with the landowners around it.

484
37:21.761 --> 37:24.222
They'll be done soon enough.

485
37:24.305 --> 37:26.933
Even if you're unhappy with the conditions and protest,

486
37:27.016 --> 37:30.353
Sia plans to proceed with the development of that area.

487
37:30.436 --> 37:31.646
Okay, I understand.

488
37:32.564 --> 37:34.274
Thank you.

489
37:36.651 --> 37:40.321
Yubin is manipulating and taking advantage of you, Karin.

490
37:40.947 --> 37:43.741
All he wants from you is your property.

491
37:45.076 --> 37:48.746
The sooner you stop being so stubborn, he'll be able to return home.

492
37:49.914 --> 37:51.666
Let him buy your plot of land already.

493
37:53.376 --> 37:55.128
That way, he can get back to his future.

494
37:57.797 --> 37:59.841
Shouldn't you sell Yubin your land?

495
38:01.926 --> 38:05.305
If you really care, help him get back to where he belongs.

496
38:13.688 --> 38:15.273
[in Korean] Han Sia.

497
38:17.942 --> 38:18.943
We need to talk.

498
38:19.819 --> 38:20.820
Why not.

499
38:33.625 --> 38:34.834
What do you think you're doing?

500
38:36.878 --> 38:37.879
You heard?

501
38:37.962 --> 38:40.256
What are you planning to do with this village?

502
38:40.340 --> 38:42.759
-What's with that development plan? -[door opens]

503
38:48.848 --> 38:52.518
[in English] Same as you, I'm here to buy the land. Except, you came here first.

504
39:05.949 --> 39:08.201
-[in Korean] Stop playing games. -You're the one who needs

505
39:08.284 --> 39:09.744
-to stop playing games here. -Han Sia.

506
39:09.827 --> 39:12.538
I'm doing this with or without her land.

507
39:13.122 --> 39:16.125
I saw this place with my own eyes.

508
39:16.209 --> 39:19.253
There are many who support this development.

509
39:20.421 --> 39:22.298
This project is happening with or without you.

510
39:27.553 --> 39:30.848
This is your last chance.

511
39:35.269 --> 39:36.646
Leave already.

512
39:38.773 --> 39:40.024
If you walk away now,

513
39:41.317 --> 39:43.236
your career is over.

514
40:00.086 --> 40:02.088
[Yubin] I thought it might be because of the strawberries.

515
40:03.047 --> 40:05.425
I wanted to help out.

516
40:08.428 --> 40:13.516
I wanted to accurately represent the field you work on

517
40:13.599 --> 40:16.269
and let everyone here see it.

518
40:16.352 --> 40:18.438
Hmm. You can trust me.

519
40:29.824 --> 40:30.825
Wait.

520
40:31.951 --> 40:36.122
Karin, wait. Please hear me out.

521
40:38.249 --> 40:42.920
About earlier, I don't want you to misunderstand.

522
40:47.216 --> 40:48.801
[in English] You're not here to buy my land?

523
40:51.846 --> 40:54.348
Ah, this… land?

524
40:55.516 --> 40:56.642
[in Korean] Right, all this…

525
40:57.185 --> 40:58.311
It's true.

526
40:59.228 --> 41:01.522
At first, I came to…

527
41:01.606 --> 41:02.899
You can't understand me.

528
41:05.026 --> 41:06.611
This land…

529
41:06.694 --> 41:10.073
Wait. Please, hear me out.

530
41:10.740 --> 41:15.995
I meant to explain all this to you…

531
41:23.836 --> 41:24.837
Hey, are you okay?

532
42:08.339 --> 42:09.590
[in English] Please…

533
42:12.385 --> 42:13.636
I need you to leave.

534
42:14.971 --> 42:16.264
Get out of my house.

535
42:18.099 --> 42:19.559
Get off my land.

536
42:27.024 --> 42:28.401
But thank you…

537
42:30.862 --> 42:32.446
for everything.

538
43:15.406 --> 43:17.658
MERRY BERRY LOVE

539
43:17.742 --> 43:18.743
NEXT EPISODE

540
43:18.826 --> 43:21.078
[Sanggi, in Korean] How did you end up working for Sia's company?

541
43:22.455 --> 43:25.875
[Mari, in English] Splitting up, it's a really hard thing to go through.

542
43:26.626 --> 43:27.960
[Yubin, in Korean] Karin.

543
43:28.044 --> 43:29.128
I care about you deeply.
